  "description": "Victor Wembanyama picked a 250 million dollar deal over 300 million, so the Spurs could keep their young core.\n\nSources:\n- AP via Fox Sports (Jul 10 2026): https://www.foxsports.com/articles/nba/victor-wembanyama-san-antonio-spurs-agree-on-5year-extension-that-could-top-250m-ap-source-says\n- Wikipedia: Victor Wembanyama: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Victor_Wembanyama\n\nFrom AP (Fox Sports): on July 10 2026 Wembanyama signed a five-year Spurs extension that could exceed $250 million if the player option in the last season is picked up; he could have agreed to a deal topping $300 million over five years but chose less to give the Spurs flexibility with their young core; he makes about $16.8 million in 2026-27, the last season of his rookie contract; the new deal starts in 2027-28 at about $43.5 million. From Wikipedia: a youth coach at Nanterre noticed him on the bench at an under-11 game because of his height, 1.80 m (5 ft 11 in), mistaking him for a coach; he began his pro career at age 15 with Nanterre 92 in 2019; the Spurs picked him first overall on 22 June 2023; on 4 November 2026 he had a career-high 52 points and 24 rebounds with eight blocks, the first 50-point, 20-rebound, 5-block game since Bob McAdoo in 1974. Not financial advice.\n\n#shorts #wembanyama #spurs #howtheymakemoney",
